KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.alias]/2 + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A pack-expansion alias
template (`sums = sum_t<sizeof(Us)...>`) instantiated with a pack FORWARDED from
an enclosing function template (`sums<Us...>` where `Us` is the caller's pack)
does not fold: `chk((char)1,(char)2)` should be a constant 2 but CBMC leaves it
unconstrained (g++/clang++ compute 2).  The same alias with explicit concrete
arguments folds fine, and a non-pack-expansion alias forwards fine, so the defect
is specific to a pack-expansion alias body instantiated with a forwarded pack.
Minimal form: a free function template + namespace alias (no class needed).  This
masks the separately fixed two-parallel-pack member-alias expansion
(cpp11_alias_template_parallel_pack) and is a residual blocker for std::tuple's
_TupleConstraints.  Flip to CORE once a pack-expansion alias folds when
instantiated with a forwarded parameter pack.
